  "details": "non-public variable in another UdonBehaviour is accessible with SetProgramVariable and SetProgramVariable node. No documentations are available now, so I'm not sure this is a bug. Anyway, it's unexpected for me.\nUDONSDK-2019.12.22.12.32_Public\nVRCSDK3-2019.12.21.16.01\nI think, if Udon program user and creator are different person in the future, then maybe we need \"protected (between graphs)\" variable. It's necessarily to make reusable building blocks as another programming language does.\nCurrently Udon variable has only one boolean property \"public\". I suggest this be extended as an enumeration like:\n- public (Udon program user may change via Inspector)\n- protected (accessible between graphs. not shown in Inspector)\n- private (accessible within one UdonBehaviour that runs the graph)\n- local (accessible within a sub-graph (and/or block?). Identical name in two sub-graph refers different one)",
  "error": null,
